BT /F1 11 Tf 50 742 Td (## 2. Displacement, velocity and acceleration) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 726 Td (Average velocity is displacement divided by time: `v = ”x / ”t`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 710 Td (Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity: `a = ”v / ”t`, measured in m/s^2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 694 Td (Velocity is a vector, so reversing direction changes its sign even when the speed is constant.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 678 Td (On a displacement-time graph the slope is velocity; on a velocity-time graph the slope is acceleration and the area is displacement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 662 Td (Uniform acceleration means the velocity changes by the same amount every second.) Tj ET
endstream
