BT /F1 11 Tf 50 742 Td (Archimedes' principle: the upthrust equals the weight of fluid displaced.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 726 Td (A body floats when its average density is less than the fluid's density.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 710 Td (Worked examples:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 694 Td (- At 5 m depth in water the gauge pressure is 1000 × 9.8 × 5 = 49 000 Pa.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 678 Td (- A 2 kg block of volume 0.001 m^3 has density 2000 kg/m^3 and sinks in water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 50 662 Td (Remember: this topic contributed 14 questions in last year's paper, and the examiner marked the unit errors strictly.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
